---
description: User-facing UI errors must be specific and actionable
alwaysApply: true
---

# Clear error messages

Never show vague copy like `Something went wrong`, `An error occurred`, `Request failed`, or `Error`.

## Do

- Prefer the backend `message` from axios / react-query errors (do not replace it with a generic toast)
- For client-side validation / preflight failures, name the field and the fix
- Empty/error states: say what failed to load and offer retry when possible

## Don't

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
Toast("Something went wrong", "error");
setError("An error occurred");

// ✅ GOOD
Toast("Select a payment method before continuing.", "error");
setError("Could not load your dues. Check your connection and retry.");
```

When the API already returned a clear `message`, do not toast a second generic line on top of it.
